/**
 * ชังชัง, the guide who stands beside the waste-sorting game.
 *
 * ONE LONG LINE OF BASE64, and it is here rather than in `assets/` on purpose.
 * The game is an HTML page handed to a WebView as a string, and a WebView
 * given bare HTML has no origin to resolve `assets/buddy.png` against. The
 * ways out are an absolute URL to the asset server - which is cleartext http
 * in Expo Go, so Android blocks it as mixed content on an https page - or
 * putting the bytes in the document. A `data:` URI is neither fetched nor
 * blocked, works with no network at all, and is the only one of the three
 * that cannot fail on somebody's phone in a place with no signal.
 *
 * WebP because the artwork has a soft alpha edge. The same picture as an RGBA
 * PNG is 222 KB and as a quantised PNG it grows a halo where the drop shadow
 * fades out; WebP keeps the edge and costs 44 KB. Nothing in React Native
 * decodes this - it is read by the browser inside the WebView, where WebP has
 * been supported since iOS 14 and long before that on Android.
 *
 * Re-made from the 1190x1322 original with:
 *   im.resize((440, 489), LANCZOS).save(out, 'WEBP', quality=82, method=6)
 * 440 is wide enough: the page draws it at 260 CSS px at the very largest and
 * at 86 px on a phone.
 *
 * This is the ONLY place the mascot appears. The card on the game tab is the
 * app's own type and colour, because ChivarGo has its own companions and
 * mascots and whether ชังชัง joins them is a decision about the brand that
 * nobody has made yet. Until somebody does, the character stays inside the
 * game, which is where it arrived.
 */

export const WASTE_SORT_BUDDY = 'data:image/webp;base64,';
